198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10048,2900,429,279,3245,4185,5248,315,279,1156,400,17,20,3,6785,25780,374,6144,311,400,17,21,32,22,16,16,19,33,19,34,15,12947,7379,400,16,15,15,1124,15136,362,488,220,16,15,1124,15136,425,488,356,12947,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSuppose that the least common multiple of the first $25$ positive integers is equal to $26A7114B4C0$. Find $100 \\times A + 10 \\times B + C$.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"e7465922015f399a7547e7c1d07849b854c39af7af6272375cf9401c54a455e0"},"seconds":66.53460168838501,"seed":373461019096731014,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of the first 25 positive integers and then determine the digits \\(A\\), \\(B\\), and \\(C\\) in the given number \\(26A7114B4C0\\). Finally, we will compute \\(100 \\times A + 10 \\times B + C\\).\n\n### Step 1: Determine the LCM of the first 25 positive integers\nThe LCM of a set of numbers is the smallest number that is a multiple of each of the numbers in the set. To find the LCM of the first 25 positive integers, we need to consider the highest powers of all prime numbers less than or equal to 25.\n\nThe prime numbers less than or equal to 25 are: \\(2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23\\).\n\n- Highest power of 2: \\(2^4 = 16\\) (since \\(2^5 = 32 > 25\\))\n- Highest power of 3: \\(3^2 = 9\\) (since \\(3^3 = 27 > 25\\))\n- Highest power of 5: \\(5^2 = 25\\) (since \\(5^3 = 125 > 25\\))\n- Highest power of 7: \\(7^1 = 7\\) (since \\(7^2 = 49 > 25\\))\n- Highest power of 11: \\(11^1 = 11\\) (since \\(11^2 = 121 > 25\\))\n- Highest power of 13: \\(13^1 = 13\\) (since \\(13^2 = 169 > 25\\))\n- Highest power of 17: \\(17^1 = 17\\) (since \\(17^2 = 289 > 25\\))\n- Highest power of 19: \\(19^1 = 19\\) (since \\(19^2 = 361 > 25\\))\n- Highest power of 23: \\(23^1 = 23\\) (since \\(23^2 = 529 > 25\\))\n\nThus, the LCM of the first 25 positive integers is:\n\\[\n2^4 \\times 3^2 \\times 5^2 \\times 7 \\times 11 \\times 13 \\times 17 \\times 19 \\times 23\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the LCM\nWe calculate the product step by step:\n\\[\n2^4 = 16\n\\]\n\\[\n3^2 = 9\n\\]\n\\[\n5^2 = 25\n\\]\n\\[\n7 = 7\n\\]\n\\[\n11 = 11\n\\]\n\\[\n13 = 13\n\\]\n\\[\n17 = 17\n\\]\n\\[\n19 = 19\n\\]\n\\[\n23 = 23\n\\]\n\nNow, we multiply these together:\n\\[\n16 \\times 9 = 144\n\\]\n\\[\n144 \\times 25 = 3600\n\\]\n\\[\n3600 \\times 7 = 25200\n\\]\n\\[\n25200 \\times 11 = 277200\n\\]\n\\[\n277200 \\times 13 = 3603600\n\\]\n\\[\n3603600 \\times 17 = 61261200\n\\]\n\\[\n61261200 \\times 19 = 1163962800\n\\]\n\\[\n1163962800 \\times 23 = 26771144400\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Match the LCM with the given number\nThe LCM \\(26771144400\\) matches the given number \\(26A7114B4C0\\). By comparing the two numbers, we identify:\n\\[\nA = 7, \\quad B = 4, \\quad C = 4\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Compute \\(100 \\times A + 10 \\times B + C\\)\n\\[\n100 \\times 7 + 10 \\times 4 + 4 = 700 + 40 + 4 = 744\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{744}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{744}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
